   "words": [4.23],
   "part": "scene-8/1"
  },
  {
   "id": "L01",
   "file": "swiftee-lesson-1",
   "use": "lesson",
   "text": "Look! A point.",
   "start": 0.1,
   "end": 1.67,
   "words": [0.1, 1.14, 1.2]
  },
  {
   "id": "L02",
   "file": "swiftee-lesson-1",
   "use": "lesson",
   "text": "Woah! It drew a shape.",
   "start": 2.57,
   "end": 5.01,
   "words": [2.57, 4.0, 4.18, 4.46, 4.7]
  },
  {
   "id": "L03",
   "file": "swiftee-lesson-1",
   "use": "lesson",
   "text": "Let's look at this shape closely.",
   "start": 5.9,
   "end": 7.75,
   "words": [5.9, 6.22, 6.42, 6.6, 6.78, 7.22]
  },
  {
   "id": "L04",
   "file": "swiftee-lesson-1",
   "use": "lesson",
   "text": "There are no gaps in its boundary.",
   "start": 8.75,
   "end": 10.74,
   "words": [8.75, 8.96, 9.12, 9.38, 9.8, 10.02, 10.2]
  },
  {
   "id": "L05",
   "file": "swiftee-lesson-1",
   "use": "lesson",
   "text": "Is it open or closed?",
   "start": 11.58,
   "end": 13.63,
   "words": [11.58, 11.72, 12.3, 12.79, 12.96]
  },
  {
   "id": "L06",
   "file": "swiftee-lesson-1",
   "use": "lesson",
   "text": "No gaps in its boundary. This shape is closed.",
   "start": 14.8,
   "end": 18.73,
   "words": [14.8, 15.06, 15.44, 15.68, 15.84, 17.07, 17.32, 17.93, 18.1]
  },
  {
   "id": "L07",
   "file": "swiftee-lesson-1",
   "use": "lesson",
   "text": "There is a gap in its boundary. It is open.",
   "start": 19.9,
   "end": 22.82,
   "words": [19.9, 20.1, 20.24, 20.42, 20.74, 20.88, 21.08, 22.2, 22.32, 22.68]
  },
  {
   "id": "L08",
   "file": "swiftee-lesson-1",
   "use": "lesson",
   "text": "Yes! It is closed.",
   "start": 23.84,
   "end": 25.87,
   "words": [23.84, 24.83, 24.94, 25.23]
  },
  {
   "id": "L09",
   "file": "swiftee-lesson-1",
   "use": "lesson",
   "text": "Yes! It is open.",
   "start": 26.42,
   "end": 28.13,
   "words": [26.42, 27.37, 27.52, 27.68]
  },
  {
   "id": "L10",
   "file": "swiftee-lesson-1",
   "use": "lesson",
   "text": "Is this shape open or closed?",
   "start": 29.2,
   "end": 31.48,
   "words": [29.2, 29.36, 29.62, 30.12, 30.42, 30.8]
  },
  {
   "id": "L11",
   "file": "swiftee-lesson-1",
   "use": "lesson",
   "text": "What about this one?",
   "start": 32.35,
   "end": 33.42,
   "words": [32.35, 32.52, 32.82, 33.08]
  },
  {
   "id": "L12",
   "file": "swiftee-lesson-1",
   "use": "lesson",
   "text": "And this?",
   "start": 33.98,
   "end": 34.67,
   "words": [33.98, 34.2]
  },
  {
   "id": "L13",
   "file": "swiftee-lesson-1",
   "use": "lesson",
   "text": "How about this one?",
   "start": 35.59,
   "end": 36.8,
   "words": [35.59, 35.76, 36.2, 36.4]
  },
  {
   "id": "L14",
   "file": "swiftee-lesson-1",
   "use": "lesson",
   "text": "These two shapes are open...",
   "start": 37.67,
   "end": 39.52,
   "words": [37.67, 37.98, 38.28, 38.7, 39.0]
  },
  {
   "id": "L15",
   "file": "swiftee-lesson-1",
   "use": "lesson",
   "text": "...and these two shapes are closed.",
   "start": 40.22,
   "end": 42.34,
   "words": [40.22, 40.44, 40.7, 40.98, 41.38, 41.74]
  },
  {
   "id": "L16",
   "file": "swiftee-lesson-1",
   "use": "lesson",
   "text": "Look! The boundaries of the shapes are different too.",
   "start": 43.32,
   "end": 46.49,
   "words": [43.32, 44.09, 44.28, 44.7, 44.98, 45.14, 45.44, 45.68, 45.98]
  },
  {
   "id": "L17",
   "file": "swiftee-lesson-1",
   "use": "lesson",
   "text": "Some are straight and some are curved.",
   "start": 47.14,
   "end": 49.35,
   "words": [47.14, 47.42, 47.64, 48.25, 48.42, 48.64, 48.9]
  },
  {
   "id": "L18",
   "file": "swiftee-lesson-1",
   "use": "lesson",
   "text": "Which boundaries are straight and which are curved?",
   "start": 50.08,
   "end": 53.09,
   "words": [50.08, 50.3, 50.8, 51.18, 52.02, 52.18, 52.34, 52.64],
   "unrecognised": ["curved?"]
  },
  {
   "id": "L19",
   "file": "swiftee-lesson-1",
   "use": "lesson",
   "text": "Look! This boundary isn't curved. It is made of straight lines.",
   "start": 54.19,
   "end": 58.63,
   "words": [54.19, 54.92, 55.16, 55.64, 56.06, 57.01, 57.12, 57.32, 57.5, 57.72, 58.0]
  },
  {
   "id": "L20",
   "file": "swiftee-lesson-1",
   "use": "lesson",
   "text": "Look closely. This boundary bends smoothly. It is curved.",
   "start": 59.4,
   "end": 64.0,
   "words": [59.4, 59.64, 60.48, 60.78, 61.28, 61.8, 63.15, 63.26, 63.48]
  },
  {
   "id": "L21",
   "file": "swiftee-lesson-1",
   "use": "lesson",
   "text": "Is the boundary straight or curved?",
   "start": 64.71,
   "end": 66.81,
   "words": [64.71, 64.86, 65.08, 65.4, 66.07, 66.26]
  },
  {
   "id": "L22",
   "file": "swiftee-lesson-1",
   "use": "lesson",
   "text": "You got it! These boundaries are straight, while these are curved.",
   "start": 67.76,
   "end": 72.09,
   "words": [67.76, 67.9, 68.08, 68.86, 69.16, 69.6, 69.98, 70.65, 70.84, 71.24, 71.52]
  },
  {
   "id": "L23",
   "file": "swiftee-lesson-1",
   "use": "lesson",
   "text": "Tap the closed figure made with straight lines.",
   "start": 73.15,
   "end": 75.71,
   "words": [73.15, 73.47, 73.64, 73.96, 74.3, 74.58, 74.84, 75.1]
  },
  {
   "id": "L24",
   "file": "swiftee-lesson-1",
   "use": "lesson",
   "text": "Yes! It is closed and made of straight lines.",
   "start": 76.43,
   "end": 79.95,
   "words": [76.43, 77.5, 77.62, 77.88, 78.26, 78.56, 78.8, 79.04, 79.28]
  },
  {
   "id": "L25",
   "file": "swiftee-lesson-1",
   "use": "lesson",
   "text": "Not quite. Look for a figure with no gaps and no curves.",
   "start": 80.76,
   "end": 84.76,
   "words": [80.76, 80.98, 82.09, 82.26, 82.46, 82.62, 82.82, 83.02, 83.34, 83.7, 83.94, 84.16]
  },
  {
   "id": "L26",
   "file": "swiftee-lesson-1",
   "use": "lesson",
   "text": "We call this a polygon.",
   "start": 85.27,
   "end": 87.07,
   "words": [85.27, 85.44, 85.74, 86.3, 86.52]
  },
  {
   "id": "L27",
   "file": "swiftee-lesson-1",
   "use": "lesson",
   "text": "A closed figure made of only straight line segments is called a polygon.",
   "start": 87.69,
   "end": 92.12,
   "words": [87.69, 87.82, 88.28, 88.6, 88.84, 89.06, 89.36, 89.76, 90.08, 90.5, 90.82, 91.16, 91.44]
  },
  {
   "id": "L28",
   "file": "swiftee-lesson-1",
   "use": "lesson",
   "text": "Which of these figures are polygons?",
   "start": 92.75,
   "end": 94.57,
   "words": [92.75, 92.92, 93.08, 93.34, 93.6, 93.84]
  },
  {
   "id": "L29",
   "file": "swiftee-lesson-1",
   "use": "lesson",
   "text": "Great job! You identified all the polygons.",
   "start": 95.84,
   "end": 99.08,
   "words": [95.84, 96.18, 96.86, 97.0, 97.89, 98.16, 98.38]
  },
  {
   "id": "L30",
   "file": "swiftee-lesson-1",
   "use": "lesson",
   "text": "A polygon is closed, with only straight sides.",
   "start": 99.58,
   "end": 102.95,
   "words": [99.58, 99.72, 100.18, 100.44, 101.25, 101.38, 101.8, 102.24]
  },
  {
   "id": "L31",
   "file": "swiftee-lesson-1",
   "use": "lesson",
   "text": "These line segments are the sides of the polygon.",
   "start": 103.63,
   "end": 106.23,
   "words": [103.63, 103.9, 104.22, 104.6, 104.86, 105.04, 105.4, 105.56, 105.74]
  },
  {
   "id": "L32",
   "file": "swiftee-lesson-1",
   "use": "lesson",
   "text": "The point where two sides meet is called a vertex.",
   "start": 106.91,
   "end": 109.89,
   "words": [106.91, 107.02, 107.3, 107.54, 107.84, 108.22, 108.52, 108.82, 109.18, 109.5]
  },
  {
   "id": "L33",
   "file": "swiftee-lesson-1",
   "use": "lesson",
   "text": "When two sides meet, they also form an angle.",
   "start": 110.96,
   "end": 113.79,
   "words": [110.96, 111.1, 111.44, 111.76, 112.38, 112.54, 112.84, 113.24, 113.44]
  },
  {
   "id": "L34",
   "file": "swiftee-lesson-1",
   "use": "lesson",
   "text": "Label the parts of the polygon.",
   "start": 114.56,
   "end": 116.07,
   "words": [114.56, 114.82, 115.04, 115.32, 115.46, 115.62]
  },
  {
   "id": "L35",
   "file": "swiftee-lesson-1",
   "use": "lesson",
   "text": "Perfect! Side, vertex and angle — all labelled.",
   "start": 116.88,
   "end": 121.32,
   "words": [116.88, 117.75, 118.51, 118.92, 119.42, null, 120.27, 120.64]
  },
  {
   "id": "L36",
   "file": "swiftee-lesson-1",
   "use": "lesson",
   "text": "Let's count the sides of the polygon.",
   "start": 122.13,
   "end": 123.88,
   "words": [122.13, 122.4, 122.6, 122.8, 123.1, 123.24, 123.4]
  },
  {
   "id": "L37",
   "file": "swiftee-lesson-1",
   "use": "lesson",
   "text": "Count each side carefully and try again.",
   "start": 124.52,
   "end": 127.15,
   "words": [124.52, 124.78, 125.12, 125.46, 126.27, 126.4, 126.64]
  },
  {
   "id": "L38",
   "file": "swiftee-lesson-1",
   "use": "lesson",
   "text": "Correct! This polygon has five sides.",
   "start": 128.16,
   "end": 131.16,
   "words": [128.16, 129.15, 129.42, 129.9, 130.37, 130.66]
  },
  {
   "id": "L39",
   "file": "swiftee-lesson-1",
   "use": "lesson",
   "text": "Now let's change how it looks.",
   "start": 132.25,
   "end": 133.67,
   "words": [132.25, 132.46, 132.76, 133.12, 133.36, 133.52]
  },
  {
   "id": "L40",
   "file": "swiftee-lesson-1",
   "use": "lesson",
   "text": "Drag any vertex. Stretch it, squash it, or resize it.",
   "start": 134.57,
   "end": 139.33,
   "words": [134.57, 134.94, 135.42, 136.73, 137.06, 137.51, 137.86, 138.38, 138.56, 138.98]
  },
  {
   "id": "L41",
   "file": "swiftee-lesson-1",
   "use": "lesson",
   "text": "Whoa! It looks quite different now.",
   "start": 140.13,
   "end": 142.57,
   "words": [140.13, 141.15, 141.26, 141.46, 141.72, 142.14]
  },
  {
   "id": "L42",
   "file": "swiftee-lesson-1",
   "use": "lesson",
   "text": "Its appearance has completely changed.",
   "start": 143.11,
   "end": 145.13,
   "words": [143.11, 143.46, 143.7, 144.02, 144.54]
  },
  {
   "id": "L43",
   "file": "swiftee-lesson-1",
   "use": "lesson",
   "text": "But not everything has changed.",
   "start": 145.92,
   "end": 147.68,
   "words": [145.92, 146.04, 146.3, 146.82, 147.12]
  },
  {
   "id": "L44",
   "file": "swiftee-lesson-1",
   "use": "lesson",
   "text": "Let's count the sides again.",
   "start": 148.3,
   "end": 149.73,
   "words": [148.3, 148.58, 148.8, 149.02, 149.3]
  },
  {
   "id": "L45",
   "file": "swiftee-lesson-1",
   "use": "lesson",
   "text": "Both polygons still have five sides.",
   "start": 150.31,
   "end": 152.95,
   "words": [150.31, 150.56, 151.14, 151.56, 152.06, 152.32]
  },
  {
   "id": "L46",
   "file": "swiftee-lesson-1",
   "use": "lesson",
   "text": "So the number of sides gives us a good way to name polygons.",
   "start": 153.61,
   "end": 156.87,
   "words": [153.61, 153.76, 153.92, 154.16, 154.4, 154.76, 155.0, 155.14, 155.28, 155.44, 155.66, 155.9, 156.12]
  },
  {
   "id": "L47",
   "file": "swiftee-lesson-1",
   "use": "lesson",
   "text": "A polygon with three sides is called a triangle.",
   "start": 157.5,
   "end": 160.4,
   "words": [157.5, 157.62, 158.08, 158.33, 158.56, 159.08, 159.38, 159.66, 159.9]
  },
  {
   "id": "L48",
   "file": "swiftee-lesson-1",
   "use": "lesson",
   "text": "A polygon with four sides is called a quadrilateral.",
   "start": 160.93,
   "end": 164.17,
   "words": [160.93, 161.06, 161.44, 161.78, 161.96, 162.48, 162.72, 163.19, 163.42]
  },
  {
   "id": "L49",
   "file": "swiftee-lesson-1",
   "use": "lesson",
   "text": "Select all the quadrilaterals.",
   "start": 164.99,
   "end": 166.92,
   "words": [164.99, 165.4, 165.76, 165.98]
  },
  {
